	('de89e842-79c1-4017-9058-422019644d28', 'f77b8ee9-2759-4bbe-9bae-c281784b39d5', 'en', 'Which nerve controls the mimic muscles?', '["N. trigeminus", "N. facialis", "N. glossopharyngeus", "N. vagus"]', 'N. facialis', 'This option is correct because that nerve supplies the structure or function named in the stem.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:23.944128+00'),
	('0c1064a4-c005-4642-8f26-1fb8de6bcfbd', 'fc47340d-7439-488d-95a0-48f3c4899d6e', 'en', 'What active ingredient is a vitamin K antagonist?', '["warfarin", "heparin", "Dabigatran", "rivaroxaban"]', 'warfarin', 'warfarin is correct because it best matches the key medical fact asked in this question.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:23.944128+00'),
	('e53a7766-913d-4c07-b2c2-c72772c3d0f0', 'fd916b22-a317-44ac-a4ed-36547e3dc78f', 'en', 'Which pathogen causes Legionella pneumonia?', '["Legionella pneumophila", "chlamydia trachomatis", "Bordetella pertussis", "Coxiella burnetii"]', 'Legionella pneumophila', 'This option is correct because it is the classic pathogen or infection associated with the condition named in the stem.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:23.944128+00'),
	('e4ee7a88-f470-4d4d-b74f-811ac1fc9eb5', 'fdfa6af3-13a5-45dc-a782-4e6681a0060d', 'en', 'What structure separates right and left atrium?', '["Precinct septum", "ventricle septum", "Aortic flap", "Tricuspidal flap"]', 'Precinct septum', 'This option is correct because that structure fulfills the anatomical role asked for in the question.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:23.944128+00'),
	('bc39652b-6f24-4cfd-83e9-0ef734e58a14', 'fff09c95-24d3-4995-afda-6fc40d188d03', 'en', 'Which bone forms the front end of the thorax and connects the rib pairs?', '["star", "Clavicula", "Scapula", "humus"]', 'star', 'star is correct because it best matches the key medical fact asked in this question.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.564239+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:23.944128+00'),
	('e93902b9-aae9-46eb-a977-10211e410013', '8c37b29d-53d4-466a-8830-5e9409e46373', 'de', 'Wie heisst der Knochen des Unterarms auf der Daumenseite?', '["Radius", "Ulna", "Humerus", "Fibula"]', 'Radius', 'Der Radius liegt in anatomischer Grundstellung auf der Daumenseite des Unterarms. Die Ulna liegt dagegen auf der Kleinfingerseite.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('c57dabff-1940-4b0c-b24f-077d535d2234', 'd716bcb6-9316-4556-a885-3e20b506a9bf', 'de', 'Welche Struktur verläuft durch den Canalis carpi?', '["N. medianus", "N. ulnaris", "N. radialis", "N. musculocutaneus"]', 'N. medianus', 'Durch den Canalis carpi ziehen der N. medianus und mehrere Beugesehnen. Wird der Nerv dort eingeengt, entsteht das typische Karpaltunnelsyndrom.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('da64b3d3-f4b8-47a7-9306-4bbbbeca46c6', '43e0a3d9-1ef4-486a-a62a-1d1a8a1b8922', 'de', 'Welche Arterie versorgt die Milz?', '["A. splenica", "A. hepatica", "A. renalis", "A. mesenterica inferior"]', 'A. splenica', 'Die A. splenica entspringt aus dem Truncus coeliacus und zieht entlang des Pankreas zur Milz. Sie ist die arterielle Hauptversorgung der Milz.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('514b7bb7-1434-4696-b358-e8d8ca3572e3', 'da985737-a75e-4877-9b54-589b998542d3', 'de', 'Welches Hormon erhöht die Herzfrequenz akut?', '["Adrenalin", "Insulin", "Cortisol", "Prolaktin"]', 'Adrenalin', 'Adrenalin aktiviert am Herzen vor allem Beta-1-Rezeptoren. Dadurch steigen Herzfrequenz und Kontraktilitaet innerhalb kurzer Zeit an.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('a47eb9d3-2b7b-4c32-851d-6be5983c80c6', '2d67e8f7-5d65-42b3-a354-93b3b020fda4', 'de', 'Wo wird ADH gespeichert und freigesetzt?', '["Neurohypophyse", "Adenohypophyse", "Nebennierenrinde", "Schilddrüse"]', 'Neurohypophyse', 'ADH wird im Hypothalamus gebildet, aber in der Neurohypophyse gespeichert und von dort freigesetzt. Genau nach diesem Speicher- und Freisetzungsort fragt die Aufgabe.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('d67deffe-83e1-441a-8493-95da25f612f9', 'b59913c1-62c1-40b9-9538-2a0a4a123f99', 'de', 'Welcher Transporter ist für Glukoseaufnahme in Muskel insulinabhängig?', '["GLUT4", "GLUT1", "GLUT2", "SGLT1"]', 'GLUT4', 'GLUT4 ist der insulinabhaengige Glukosetransporter in Muskel- und Fettzellen. Nach Insulinwirkung wird er in die Zellmembran eingebaut und steigert dort die Glukoseaufnahme.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('991eac29-47ca-4763-80b6-638f3c398278', '6d7668c9-7cbc-4bc3-81db-26845ed38cc8', 'de', 'Wie nennt man eine Entzündung der Bauchspeicheldrüse?', '["Pankreatitis", "Hepatitis", "Appendizitis", "Gastritis"]', 'Pankreatitis', 'Die Endung -itis bezeichnet eine Entzuendung. Zusammen mit Pankreas ergibt sich deshalb Pankreatitis als korrekter Fachbegriff.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('fcf78abb-4401-47bd-b04f-baee05aea889', 'e62554d8-4aa8-4773-bedf-ba209f4c3155', 'de', 'Welche Nekroseform ist typisch beim Hirninfarkt?', '["Kolliquationsnekrose", "Koagulationsnekrose", "Fettgewebsnekrose", "Fibrinoidnekrose"]', 'Kolliquationsnekrose', 'Im Gehirn entsteht nach einem Infarkt typischerweise eine Kolliquationsnekrose. Das Gewebe wird enzymatisch verfluessigt, statt seine Architektur wie bei der Koagulationsnekrose zu behalten.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('da40dd45-b8ee-4d01-8a34-8fafc2edb9a3', '14005380-03c2-4df1-9389-a5eb2664f4db', 'de', 'Welche Mutation ist typisch beim Li-Fraumeni-Syndrom?', '["p53", "BRCA1", "APC", "RB1"]', 'p53', 'Das Li-Fraumeni-Syndrom beruht meist auf Keimbahnmutationen in TP53. Faellt p53 aus, gehen wichtige Kontrollen von DNA-Schaeden und Zellzyklus verloren.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('4ecbc4c3-40ba-4a9a-88e3-f10e204cef82', '4768832f-7e99-4deb-8a83-dc52156f644e', 'de', 'Welcher Wirkstoff ist ein ACE-Hemmer?', '["Enalapril", "Amlodipin", "Bisoprolol", "Furosemid"]', 'Enalapril', 'Enalapril gehoert an der Endung -pril zur Gruppe der ACE-Hemmer. Diese blockieren die Umwandlung von Angiotensin I in Angiotensin II.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('172bc7f3-35f7-4280-8964-a9305c854ff3', 'bdfeed5e-3343-487b-8e7d-411954b1ee6b', 'de', 'Welches Antibiotikum hemmt die bakterielle Proteinsynthese an der 30S-Untereinheit?', '["Doxycyclin", "Erythromycin", "Vancomycin", "Ceftriaxon"]', 'Doxycyclin', 'Doxycyclin ist ein Tetracyclin und bindet an die 30S-Untereinheit bakterieller Ribosomen. Dadurch wird die Proteinsynthese gehemmt.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('972f6bf4-a290-4473-a42e-39ed347c3850', 'd891ebb6-df24-4e7c-b8a4-e6cc24bf7140', 'de', 'Welches Antidot wird bei Heparin-Überdosierung gegeben?', '["Protamin", "Naloxon", "Flumazenil", "Vitamin K"]', 'Protamin', 'Protamin ist stark positiv geladen und bindet dadurch das negativ geladene Heparin. So wird die antikoagulatorische Wirkung rasch neutralisiert.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('7c6a66b5-b1e5-4f2c-8ba6-ff014f2646e2', 'dd1d76f4-3b44-4b1f-a9a5-9002e5814739', 'de', 'Welcher Erreger verursacht typischerweise Scharlach?', '["Streptococcus pyogenes", "Staphylococcus aureus", "Haemophilus influenzae", "Neisseria meningitidis"]', 'Streptococcus pyogenes', 'Scharlach wird durch toxinbildende Staemme von Streptococcus pyogenes verursacht. Das erythrogene Toxin erklaert Exanthem und Himbeerzunge.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('01ffd530-349a-446f-9889-366abdf9dc33', '7f723e0e-7418-445d-b828-16a17d06b6a0', 'de', 'Welcher Erreger ist obligat intrazellulär?', '["Chlamydia trachomatis", "Escherichia coli", "Staphylococcus aureus", "Pseudomonas aeruginosa"]', 'Chlamydia trachomatis', 'Chlamydia trachomatis ist obligat intrazellulaer, weil der Erreger fuer seinen Stoffwechsel auf die Wirtszelle angewiesen ist. Deshalb kann er sich nicht frei ausserhalb von Zellen vermehren.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('3b7d3c5a-c0ac-47ca-89d3-2039c70837b5', '9b52a4fc-5571-43cf-9097-48b513f45910', 'de', 'Welches Toxin verursacht Pseudomembranen bei Diphtherie?', '["Diphtherietoxin", "Tetanustoxin", "Botulinumtoxin", "Exotoxin A"]', 'Diphtherietoxin', 'Das Diphtherietoxin hemmt den Elongationsfaktor 2 und stoppt so die Proteinsynthese. Lokal fuehrt das zu Nekrosen und den typischen Pseudomembranen.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('b62e3675-0340-406f-8448-1fdf5d3e1408', '4bf12282-1e93-476f-90c2-64432f730e33', 'de', 'Welche Reaktion katalysiert die ATP-Synthase?', '["ADP + Pi -> ATP", "ATP -> ADP + Pi", "Glukose -> Pyruvat", "Pyruvat -> Laktat"]', 'ADP + Pi -> ATP', 'Die ATP-Synthase nutzt den Protonengradienten der inneren Mitochondrienmembran, um ADP und anorganisches Phosphat zu ATP zusammenzufuegen. Genau diese Reaktion katalysiert sie.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('1c149093-01cc-480d-bb98-419abd04369c', 'addfc16e-a0aa-4b00-adcd-1ef7f669b06e', 'de', 'Welcher Zyklus oxidiert Acetyl-CoA?', '["Citratzyklus", "Harnstoffzyklus", "Glykolyse", "Pentosephosphatweg"]', 'Citratzyklus', 'Der Citratzyklus oxidiert Acetyl-CoA zu CO2 und liefert dabei NADH und FADH2 fuer die Atmungskette. Deshalb ist er das zentrale oxidative Stoffwechselrad.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('05f3476e-b96b-44aa-8b0f-658814b2c27a', '5240cf6b-86ff-4a98-9ccf-b7ad83ba3f88', 'de', 'Welches Molekül ist Endprodukt der Glykolyse?', '["Pyruvat", "Laktat", "Acetyl-CoA", "Oxalacetat"]', 'Pyruvat', 'Die Glykolyse endet mit Pyruvat. Laktat entsteht erst anschliessend aus Pyruvat, wenn der Stoffwechsel auf anaerobe Bedingungen ausweicht.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('197de757-5322-4f47-9efa-8a6a2c2ff4e4', '11ebf331-4492-4607-9a51-c5fb03d66422', 'de', 'Welche Zellen präsentieren Antigen über MHC II?', '["Dendritische Zellen", "Erythrozyten", "Thrombozyten", "Neurone"]', 'Dendritische Zellen', 'Dendritische Zellen sind professionelle antigenpraesentierende Zellen. Sie praesentieren Peptide ueber MHC II und aktivieren dadurch naive CD4-T-Zellen.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('2a21946f-3fc2-44bb-97f8-a25f740b3ece', '6f39bac3-747c-4c2a-9299-7d2e74306708', 'de', 'Welche Zellen vermitteln zytotoxische Abwehr?', '["CD8 T-Zellen", "B-Zellen", "Neutrophile", "Makrophagen"]', 'CD8 T-Zellen', 'CD8-T-Zellen erkennen Antigene ueber MHC I und toeten infizierte oder entartete Zellen. Damit tragen sie die klassische zytotoxische Abwehr.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('2f9b806b-de8a-4908-9a11-2951a40ec7c6', '86b49522-4c45-4f87-8960-9eb4c5584224', 'de', 'Welches Zytokin ist zentral für die Th1-Antwort?', '["IFN-gamma", "IL-4", "IL-10", "TGF-beta"]', 'IFN-gamma', 'IFN-gamma aktiviert Makrophagen und foerdert die zellulaere Immunantwort. Deshalb ist es ein Schluesselzytokin der Th1-Antwort.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('e511459c-13a7-4a68-bd3d-b1b5101f13b6', '3ede9e2f-8192-4056-b080-d08e9add3356', 'de', 'Wie viele Chromosomen hat der Mensch?', '["46", "44", "48", "52"]', '46', 'Der Mensch besitzt in somatischen Zellen 46 Chromosomen, also 23 Paare. Je ein Chromosom eines Paares stammt von jedem Elternteil.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('4b3ca2a0-1519-4c94-95b5-053657aa9852', '475570da-a756-4514-8540-3bd9aabe065c', 'de', 'Wie nennt man das Fehlen eines Chromosoms?', '["Monosomie", "Trisomie", "Deletion", "Duplikation"]', 'Monosomie', 'Bei einer Monosomie fehlt ein Chromosom aus einem normalen Paar. Im Gegensatz dazu liegt bei einer Trisomie eines zu viel vor.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('bd842a1a-80e3-4d61-98a3-614003ff0bb4', 'fe8d20ad-9041-4668-b650-eed38c55cf97', 'de', 'Welche Mutation führt zur Sichelzellanämie?', '["Glu->Val in beta-Globin", "Trinukleotid-Expansion", "Frameshift in BRCA1", "Deletion von Exon 7"]', 'Glu->Val in beta-Globin', 'Die Sichelzellanamie entsteht klassisch durch einen Austausch von Glutamat gegen Valin im Beta-Globin. Dadurch polymerisiert desoxygeniertes HbS leichter und verformt Erythrozyten sichelfoermig.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('c8312c95-ae90-4763-b0fd-0a4f70ad7aa6', 'b94149ff-4da5-4df5-a31b-4317537a7cff', 'de', 'Welche Bildgebung ist erste Wahl bei Verdacht auf Fraktur?', '["Röntgen", "CT", "MRI", "Ultraschall"]', 'Röntgen', 'Roentgen ist bei Frakturverdacht meist die erste Wahl, weil es schnell verfuegbar, guenstig und sehr gut fuer die Beurteilung knoecherner Strukturen geeignet ist.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('ad15a504-3adf-43a1-ba3f-681a59609830', '0abccbf9-4dc2-4f8b-9c29-1ed73be316d8', 'de', 'Welches Kontrastmittel wird beim CT häufig verwendet?', '["Iodhaltiges Kontrastmittel", "Gadolinium", "Barium für MRI", "Luft"]', 'Iodhaltiges Kontrastmittel', 'Beim CT werden meist iodhaltige Kontrastmittel verwendet, weil Iod als Element mit hoher Ordnungszahl Roentgenstrahlen stark abschwaecht. Dadurch heben sich Gefaesse und gut durchblutete Gewebe im CT deutlich besser ab.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('9535d8d8-3e7f-4d74-a9b0-12d5ee6ae4ad', '4dd7693d-c8bf-45ff-b04c-b1e58ea5d6a0', 'de', 'Welche MRT-Sequenz zeigt Fett hell?', '["T1", "T2", "STIR", "DWI"]', 'T1', 'In T1-Sequenzen erscheint Fett hell, weil es eine kurze T1-Relaxationszeit hat. Fluessigkeit ist in T1 dagegen eher dunkel und in T2 signalreicher.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('b1495779-2b05-4255-b66a-9e1172627c36', '12e2fcdc-2be1-4a02-af91-6c7cb056e50d', 'de', 'Wie nennt man das Entfernen des Blinddarms?', '["Appendektomie", "Cholezystektomie", "Gastrektomie", "Nephrektomie"]', 'Appendektomie', 'Die Endung -ektomie bedeutet operative Entfernung. Bei einer Appendektomie wird also der Appendix vermiformis entfernt.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('3958e026-3194-4515-987a-fc1ec8a6fd89', '8fad91c1-d7f6-4c5e-a33b-671d79ecc92c', 'de', 'Welche Narkoseform wird für grosse Bauchoperationen typischerweise genutzt?', '["Allgemeinanästhesie", "Lokalanästhesie", "Regionalanästhesie", "Sedierung ohne Analgesie"]', 'Allgemeinanästhesie', 'Groessere Bauchoperationen erfolgen meist in Allgemeinanaesthesie, weil sie sichere Atemwegskontrolle, ausreichende Analgesie und Muskelrelaxation erlaubt.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('e148bc46-4dab-4bed-aaa7-e6418bc7b13c', 'c87f4c17-8e3f-4c97-8530-66d75b51440d', 'de', 'Welche Struktur muss bei Schilddrüsen-OP besonders geschont werden?', '["N. recurrens", "N. opticus", "N. tibialis", "N. phrenicus"]', 'N. recurrens', 'Der N. recurrens innerviert die Stimmlippenmuskulatur. Wird er bei einer Schilddruesenoperation verletzt, drohen Heiserkeit oder sogar relevante Atemprobleme.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.910706+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('06d747ae-39df-494c-bf0c-5ca5c50f792d', '3ede9e2f-8192-4056-b080-d08e9add3356', 'en', 'How many chromosomes does man have?', '["46", "44", "48", "52"]', '46', 'Humans have 46 chromosomes in somatic cells, arranged as 23 pairs. One chromosome of each pair comes from each parent.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('57c191cb-15cd-4431-84c5-f776ba807e26', '8c37b29d-53d4-466a-8830-5e9409e46373', 'en', 'How is the bone of the forearm on the thumb side?', '["Radius", "Ulna", "humus", "Fibula"]', 'Radius', 'The radius lies on the thumb side of the forearm in anatomic position. The ulna lies on the little-finger side.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('30ad3759-7d28-4938-ac95-6542d48d12f6', 'd716bcb6-9316-4556-a885-3e20b506a9bf', 'en', 'What structure runs through the Canalis carpi?', '["N. medianus", "N. ulnaris", "N. radial ice", "N. musculocutaneus"]', 'N. medianus', 'The carpal tunnel contains the median nerve together with several flexor tendons. Compression there causes the typical carpal tunnel syndrome.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('c7b6109c-2bb5-442b-83ea-0fefe2890ffb', '43e0a3d9-1ef4-486a-a62a-1d1a8a1b8922', 'en', 'What artery does the spleen supply?', '["A. splenica", "A. hepatica", "A. renalis", "A. mesenterica inferior"]', 'A. splenica', 'The splenic artery arises from the celiac trunk and runs along the pancreas to the spleen. It is the main arterial supply of the spleen.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('faaac3ba-e2fc-43b7-938b-20fa9834d089', 'da985737-a75e-4877-9b54-589b998542d3', 'en', 'What hormone does the heart rate increase?', '["adrenalin", "inulin", "cortisol", "prolactin"]', 'adrenalin', 'Adrenaline mainly stimulates beta-1 receptors in the heart. That acutely increases heart rate and contractility.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('dd79af4c-b9da-4033-86ac-7307a797ac4c', '2d67e8f7-5d65-42b3-a354-93b3b020fda4', 'en', 'Where is ADH stored and released?', '["Neurohypophysis", "adenohypophysis", "Adrenal bark", "thyroid"]', 'Neurohypophysis', 'ADH is produced in the hypothalamus but stored and released from the posterior pituitary. The question specifically asks for that storage and release site.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('55e48085-b038-4fec-8457-a1552f0ba92c', 'b59913c1-62c1-40b9-9538-2a0a4a123f99', 'en', 'Which transporter is insulin-dependent for glucose absorption in muscle?', '["GLUT4", "GLUT", "GLUT", "SGLT1"]', 'GLUT4', 'GLUT4 is the insulin-dependent glucose transporter in muscle and adipose tissue. Insulin moves it into the cell membrane and thereby increases glucose uptake.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('ea3541a4-c0f5-4660-a2ce-93b7f7503965', '6d7668c9-7cbc-4bc3-81db-26845ed38cc8', 'en', 'What is called inflammation of the pancreas?', '["pancreatitis", "hepatitis", "appendizitis", "gastritis"]', 'pancreatitis', 'The suffix -itis means inflammation. Combined with pancreas, the correct medical term is pancreatitis.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('698f6738-8d9a-4eae-9f87-3aac4fde8d8b', 'e62554d8-4aa8-4773-bedf-ba209f4c3155', 'en', 'What type of necrosis is typical of brain infarction?', '["Colliquation necrosis", "Coagulation necrosis", "Fat tissue necrosis", "fibrinoid necrosis"]', 'Colliquation necrosis', 'Cerebral infarction typically causes liquefactive necrosis. Brain tissue is enzymatically digested rather than preserving its architecture as in coagulative necrosis.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('8bd52ddf-c5b5-4c86-8439-68ab15a48ac5', '14005380-03c2-4df1-9389-a5eb2664f4db', 'en', 'What mutation is typical of Li-Fraumeni syndrome?', '["p53", "BRCA1", "APC", "RB1"]', 'p53', 'Li-Fraumeni syndrome is usually caused by germline TP53 mutations. Loss of p53 removes an important checkpoint for DNA damage and the cell cycle.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('318478ce-bcd1-4bc5-a389-cb72cc08a0dc', '4768832f-7e99-4deb-8a83-dc52156f644e', 'en', 'What active ingredient is an ACE inhibitor?', '["enalapril", "amlodipine", "bisoprolol", "furosemide"]', 'enalapril', 'Enalapril belongs to the ACE inhibitor class, which is often recognized by the suffix -pril. These drugs block the conversion of angiotensin I to angiotensin II.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('b790143e-6c19-425e-a511-b2d582c21dea', 'bdfeed5e-3343-487b-8e7d-411954b1ee6b', 'en', 'What antibiotic does bacterial protein synthesis inhibit at the 30S subunit?', '["doxycycline", "erythromycin", "vancomycin", "ceftriaxone"]', 'doxycycline', 'Doxycycline is a tetracycline that binds the bacterial 30S ribosomal subunit. That inhibits bacterial protein synthesis.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('4db700c7-629b-4f7f-8fc2-51ddff888160', 'd891ebb6-df24-4e7c-b8a4-e6cc24bf7140', 'en', 'What antidote is added in heparin overdose?', '["protamine", "naloxone", "flumazenil", "Vitamin K"]', 'protamine', 'Protamine is strongly positively charged and binds negatively charged heparin. This rapidly neutralizes heparin''s anticoagulant effect.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('5bd3a44a-009a-4ca9-bfaf-e4803efd554c', 'dd1d76f4-3b44-4b1f-a9a5-9002e5814739', 'en', 'Which pathogen typically causes scarlet?', '["Streptococcus pyogenes", "Staphylococcus aureus", "Haemophilus influenzae", "Neisseria meningitidis"]', 'Streptococcus pyogenes', 'Scarlet fever is caused by toxin-producing strains of Streptococcus pyogenes. The erythrogenic toxin explains the rash and strawberry tongue.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('0e9de264-d13e-4ca9-ab7a-37096e3604a3', '7f723e0e-7418-445d-b828-16a17d06b6a0', 'en', 'Which pathogen is obligat intracellular?', '["chlamydia trachomatis", "Escherichia coli", "Staphylococcus aureus", "Pseudomonas aeruginosa"]', 'chlamydia trachomatis', 'Chlamydia trachomatis is obligately intracellular because it depends on the host cell for key metabolic functions. It cannot replicate freely outside cells.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('1bb9feea-9219-4bed-a4d3-3a53aed36dc6', '9b52a4fc-5571-43cf-9097-48b513f45910', 'en', 'What toxin causes pseudomembranes in diphtheria?', '["diphtherietoxin", "tetanus toxin", "Botulinum toxin", "Exotoxin A"]', 'diphtherietoxin', 'Diphtheria toxin inhibits elongation factor 2 and blocks protein synthesis. Locally this causes necrosis and the characteristic pseudomembranes.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('43c72858-aab0-473f-88f7-c94387c8e364', '4bf12282-1e93-476f-90c2-64432f730e33', 'en', 'What reaction does ATP synthase catalyze?', '["ADP + Pi -> ATP", "ATP -> ADP + Pi", "Glucose -> Pyruvate", "Pyruvate -> lactate"]', 'ADP + Pi -> ATP', 'ATP synthase uses the proton gradient across the inner mitochondrial membrane to join ADP and inorganic phosphate into ATP. That is the reaction it catalyzes.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('97ce837a-9614-4e31-aba6-10ecdfa04f6a', 'addfc16e-a0aa-4b00-adcd-1ef7f669b06e', 'en', 'What cycle oxidizes acetyl-CoA?', '["Citrate cycle", "Protein cycle", "glycolysis", "Pentose phosphate path"]', 'Citrate cycle', 'The citric acid cycle oxidizes acetyl-CoA to CO2 and generates NADH and FADH2 for the electron transport chain. That is why it is the central oxidative cycle of metabolism.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('27e5873c-7caa-4ad8-809f-0bcf680ae2eb', '5240cf6b-86ff-4a98-9ccf-b7ad83ba3f88', 'en', 'Which molecule is the end product of glycolysis?', '["pyruvate", "lactate", "acetyl-CoA", "oxalic acetate"]', 'pyruvate', 'Glycolysis ends with pyruvate. Lactate is formed only afterward from pyruvate when metabolism shifts toward anaerobic conditions.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('9e4160b2-c1a9-451e-948d-4fce2ed2b6b4', '11ebf331-4492-4607-9a51-c5fb03d66422', 'en', 'What cells present antigens via MHC II?', '["Dendritic cells", "erythrocytes", "thrombocytes", "Neurons"]', 'Dendritic cells', 'Dendritic cells are professional antigen-presenting cells. They present peptides on MHC II and activate naive CD4 T cells.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('fc95fcc4-33b4-4f2a-a3fc-74d6969bc2d3', '6f39bac3-747c-4c2a-9299-7d2e74306708', 'en', 'Which cells convey cytotoxic defense?', '["CD8 T cells", "B cells", "Neutrophile", "macrophages"]', 'CD8 T cells', 'CD8 T cells recognize antigen on MHC I and kill infected or malignant cells. That makes them the classic cytotoxic effector cells.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('4e5e2a3c-5d59-4e24-b427-5bc5864f2e69', '86b49522-4c45-4f87-8960-9eb4c5584224', 'en', 'Which cytokine is central to the Th1 answer?', '["IFN-gamma", "IL-4", "IL-10", "TGF-beta"]', 'IFN-gamma', 'IFN-gamma activates macrophages and promotes cell-mediated immunity. It is therefore a key cytokine of the Th1 response.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('b371e19d-e93f-4969-805e-90641e98f103', '475570da-a756-4514-8540-3bd9aabe065c', 'en', 'What do you call the absence of a chromosome?', '["Monosomie", "Trisomie", "Deletion", "Duplication"]', 'Monosomie', 'Monosomy means that one chromosome of a normal pair is missing. In contrast, trisomy means one extra chromosome is present.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('5378cdae-f3b7-4065-9777-676fd01515a2', 'fe8d20ad-9041-4668-b650-eed38c55cf97', 'en', 'What mutation leads to sickle cell anemia?', '["Glu->Val in beta-Globin", "Trinucleotide expansion", "Frameshift in BRCA1", "Deletion of Exon 7"]', 'Glu->Val in beta-Globin', 'Sickle cell disease classically results from replacement of glutamate by valine in beta-globin. This promotes polymerization of deoxygenated HbS and sickling of red cells.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('f51a2479-de38-4978-8ed4-8e5734525470', 'b94149ff-4da5-4df5-a31b-4317537a7cff', 'en', 'What picture is the first choice when suspected of fracture?', '["X", "CT", "MRI", "Ultrasound"]', 'X', 'X-ray is usually the first test for suspected fracture because it is fast, widely available, and very good for showing bone injury.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('860a2ef8-05d5-4760-bdec-ba2da4f98b46', '0abccbf9-4dc2-4f8b-9c29-1ed73be316d8', 'en', 'What contrast agent is commonly used in the CT?', '["iodine-containing contrast agent", "gadolinium", "Barium for MRI", "Air"]', 'iodine-containing contrast agent', 'CT commonly uses iodinated contrast because iodine has a high atomic number and strongly attenuates X-rays. That makes vessels and perfused tissues stand out much more clearly on CT images.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('5d8d2031-244d-477a-956c-860a0fd63b11', '4dd7693d-c8bf-45ff-b04c-b1e58ea5d6a0', 'en', 'What MRT sequence shows fat bright?', '["T1", "T2", "STIR", "DWI"]', 'T1', 'Fat appears bright on T1-weighted MRI because it has a short T1 relaxation time. Fluid is relatively dark on T1 and brighter on T2.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('65d4c433-feb9-458e-8645-b5fff96d9ce7', '12e2fcdc-2be1-4a02-af91-6c7cb056e50d', 'en', 'What is the name of removing the appendix?', '["Appendectomy", "Cholecystectomy", "Gastrectomy", "nephrectomy"]', 'Appendectomy', 'The suffix -ectomy means surgical removal. An appendectomy therefore removes the vermiform appendix.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('2f1c14d6-1a61-4a8f-9db1-2ad70536599e', '8fad91c1-d7f6-4c5e-a33b-671d79ecc92c', 'en', 'What type of anesthesia is typically used for large abdominal operations?', '["General anaesthesia", "Local anaesthesia", "Regional anaesthesia", "Sedation without analgesia"]', 'General anaesthesia', 'Major abdominal operations usually require general anesthesia because it provides airway control, analgesia, and muscle relaxation.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('ff534aab-ab6c-40b4-8810-5c1efab9af63', 'c87f4c17-8e3f-4c97-8530-66d75b51440d', 'en', 'What structure must be especially protected in thyroid surgery?', '["N. recurrens", "N. opticus", "N. tibialis", "N. phrenicus"]', 'N. recurrens', 'The recurrent laryngeal nerve innervates the vocal cord muscles. Injury during thyroid surgery can therefore cause hoarseness or significant airway problems.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.246299+00'),
	('77259615-50c4-48ab-a166-039f30a33682', 'e36e16bb-1ffc-4096-b716-0ed06d675e52', 'de', 'Welche Klappe trennt linken Vorhof und linken Ventrikel?', '["Mitralklappe", "Aortenklappe", "Trikuspidalklappe", "Pulmonalklappe"]', 'Mitralklappe', 'Mitralklappe ist richtig, weil diese Antwort die medizinische Kernaussage der Frage am besten trifft.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('e8218ed7-6650-481a-9972-59649a689fd0', 'd837ccc0-3d60-468c-b684-9c6d0eec900e', 'de', 'Welches Volumen bleibt nach maximaler Ausatmung in der Lunge?', '["Residualvolumen", "Atemzugvolumen", "Vitalkapazität", "Inspiratorisches Reservevolumen"]', 'Residualvolumen', 'Residualvolumen ist richtig, weil diese Antwort die medizinische Kernaussage der Frage am besten trifft.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('a315a86a-7516-41af-9a5c-fb4a590ead2d', '3a92ba10-07e9-43e5-bdec-df6ea5a387c4', 'de', 'Welcher Hirnabschnitt koordiniert Bewegungen?', '["Kleinhirn", "Thalamus", "Hirnstamm", "Hypothalamus"]', 'Kleinhirn', 'Kleinhirn ist richtig, weil diese Antwort die medizinische Kernaussage der Frage am besten trifft.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('f06afdde-1413-4f12-b82a-5a2db0942e3e', '7091d0d1-585a-4ae5-994e-3460b70c813b', 'de', 'Welche Zellen transportieren Sauerstoff?', '["Erythrozyten", "Leukozyten", "Thrombozyten", "Monozyten"]', 'Erythrozyten', 'Diese Antwort ist richtig, weil die genannten Zellen die im Fragetext beschriebene immunologische oder pathologische Rolle haben.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('f381e344-a5b6-407f-b32f-067ee5669563', '86a08a46-9a87-4e77-90bc-1e9417800e1b', 'de', 'Welche Struktur reguliert den Lichteinfall ins Auge?', '["Iris", "Linse", "Netzhaut", "Aderhaut"]', 'Iris', 'Diese Antwort ist richtig, weil die genannte Struktur die in der Frage gesuchte anatomische Funktion erfuellt.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('e994bc6c-408a-4b37-8308-8ed6de7146a9', '7091d0d1-585a-4ae5-994e-3460b70c813b', 'en', 'Which cells transport oxygen?', '["erythrocytes", "leukocytes", "thrombocytes", "Monozytes"]', 'erythrocytes', 'This option is correct because those cells carry out the immune or pathologic role asked about here.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('0c2f539e-e864-463f-a471-4d82ad078541', '86a08a46-9a87-4e77-90bc-1e9417800e1b', 'en', 'What structure regulates the incidence of light?', '["Iris", "lens", "recurrence", "Ader skin"]', 'Iris', 'This option is correct because that structure fulfills the anatomical role asked for in the question.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('2471d3f5-7e55-4ae9-b589-b11c3049bd70', 'd837ccc0-3d60-468c-b684-9c6d0eec900e', 'en', 'What volume remains in the lung after maximum exhalation?', '["Residual volume", "breathing volume", "Vital capacity", "Inspirator reserve volume"]', 'Residual volume', 'Residual volume is correct because it best matches the key medical fact asked in this question.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('8735bd43-fd25-43b1-bf08-5f7617027efc', 'e36e16bb-1ffc-4096-b716-0ed06d675e52', 'en', 'What flap separates left atrium and left ventricle?', '["mitral flap", "Aortic flap", "Tricuspidal flap", "Pulmonary flap"]', 'mitral flap', 'mitral flap is correct because it best matches the key medical fact asked in this question.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('d66c90f7-582e-464f-939a-072a0d35f320', 'ca6e0b05-de4c-4926-bc22-2d70f5362016', 'de', 'Welche EKG-Welle repräsentiert die Vorhoferregung?', '["P-Welle", "QRS-Komplex", "T-Welle", "U-Welle"]', 'P-Welle', 'Die P-Welle repraesentiert die Depolarisation der Vorhoefe. Erst danach folgt im QRS-Komplex die Erregung der Ventrikel.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('47e9fb43-4ae1-486f-9d6f-703e05c5bac1', '8ed37ab3-18aa-453f-a953-6e7dbb83245f', 'de', 'Welcher Muskel ist der wichtigste Atemmuskel?', '["Zwerchfell", "Interkostalmuskeln", "M. sternocleidomastoideus", "Bauchmuskeln"]', 'Zwerchfell', 'Das Zwerchfell ist der wichtigste Atemmuskel, weil seine Kontraktion den Thorax nach kaudal erweitert. Dadurch sinkt der intrathorakale Druck und Luft stroemt in die Lunge.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('1f54613d-45bd-4e87-bfa8-a96b15fbaf33', 'f3327fb0-011c-4933-b4cd-6ccf13e935ee', 'de', 'Wo findet der Gasaustausch in der Lunge statt?', '["Alveolen", "Bronchien", "Pleura", "Trachea"]', 'Alveolen', 'Der Gasaustausch findet in den Alveolen statt, weil dort eine extrem duenne Blut-Luft-Schranke besteht. So kann Sauerstoff ins Blut diffundieren und Kohlendioxid in die Ausatemluft uebertreten.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('aec1183d-3444-4228-9de5-09581ac1e5d7', 'f7ab05f5-725e-4dea-a504-8a103329a8cc', 'de', 'Wo findet die Ultrafiltration in der Niere statt?', '["Glomerulus", "Henle-Schleife", "Sammelrohr", "Distaler Tubulus"]', 'Glomerulus', 'Die Ultrafiltration findet im Glomerulus statt, wo Blut durch die Filtrationsbarriere in den Kapselraum gepresst wird. So entsteht der Primaerharn.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('e8f3a269-e3e5-4128-97ac-f78384efda84', '7aaf5d7f-6274-4781-9b68-ef8af0b1b2c0', 'de', 'Welche Struktur ist entscheidend für die Gegenstrommultiplikation?', '["Henle-Schleife", "Bowman-Kapsel", "Proximaler Tubulus", "Glomerulus"]', 'Henle-Schleife', 'Die Henle-Schleife ist entscheidend fuer die Gegenstrommultiplikation, weil ab- und aufsteigender Schenkel unterschiedliche Permeabilitaeten fuer Wasser und Salz besitzen. Dadurch entsteht der osmotische Gradient im Nierenmark.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('eda817ca-617d-486e-8ae6-44624ab7930e', '7160d588-e7b7-45d8-9018-1d1ab91b406a', 'de', 'Welches Enzym ist typisch erhöht bei cholestatischem Leberschaden?', '["Alkalische Phosphatase", "Amylase", "Troponin", "CK-MB"]', 'Alkalische Phosphatase', 'Die alkalische Phosphatase steigt bei cholestatischem Leberschaden an, weil sie vor allem im Bereich der Gallenwege vorkommt. Eine Cholestase fuehrt deshalb typischerweise zu erhoehten ALP-Werten.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('208c0556-43f2-4f6e-bb4f-14087406bf99', '09f5f514-aae2-4788-b3c1-f3c198fc4cbe', 'de', 'Welches Toxin wird in der Leber zu Harnstoff entgiftet?', '["Ammoniak", "Laktat", "Glukose", "Bilirubin"]', 'Ammoniak', 'Ammoniak wird in der Leber im Harnstoffzyklus entgiftet. Das ist wichtig, weil freies Ammoniak neurotoxisch ist und daher rasch in besser ausscheidbaren Harnstoff umgewandelt werden muss.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('db6c6e0d-47f2-40fa-ac13-0911bef1a62b', 'd25210b9-a523-49ca-b829-e65d753cbe69', 'de', 'Welcher Hirnnerv innerviert den M. rectus lateralis?', '["N. abducens (VI)", "N. oculomotorius (III)", "N. trochlearis (IV)", "N. trigeminus (V)"]', 'N. abducens (VI)', 'Der N. abducens innerviert den M. rectus lateralis und ermoeglicht damit die Abduktion des Auges. Bei einer Laesion kann das betroffene Auge nicht mehr richtig nach aussen bewegt werden.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('d7f52001-f3a5-44ee-b815-548a2af5d069', 'f9b239c6-b9ff-4aca-bb3d-78ad76eced2b', 'de', 'Welche Drüsenstruktur produziert TSH?', '["Adenohypophyse", "Neurohypophyse", "Nebennierenmark", "Schilddrüse"]', 'Adenohypophyse', 'TSH wird in der Adenohypophyse gebildet. Von dort stimuliert es die Schilddruese zur Bildung und Freisetzung von T3 und T4.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('ee584c6c-12d0-4b19-94ef-4b434f9a8c6f', 'd763b69b-0d5a-4ba2-b684-1f6de6520e7d', 'de', 'Welches Hormon wird in der Nebennierenrinde gebildet und erhöht den Blutdruck?', '["Aldosteron", "Adrenalin", "Insulin", "Glukagon"]', 'Aldosteron', 'Aldosteron wird in der Zona glomerulosa der Nebennierenrinde gebildet. Es steigert die Natrium- und Wasserretention in der Niere und kann so den Blutdruck erhoehen.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('0530c160-2745-4200-8ede-34d9e50b64dd', '46f06b2d-af16-4436-9ec3-13e69bf6a3db', 'de', 'Welches Hormon fördert die Aufnahme von Glukose in Zellen?', '["Insulin", "Glukagon", "Cortisol", "Adrenalin"]', 'Insulin', 'Insulin foerdert die Aufnahme von Glukose in Zellen, vor allem in Muskel- und Fettgewebe. Dazu bewirkt es unter anderem die Einlagerung von GLUT4 in die Zellmembran.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('e77bcd64-6a8d-4ff5-951a-e4c5861736ec', '5300bc3e-1479-4565-a1f2-ce0910cc9ead', 'de', 'Welche Struktur speichert Galle?', '["Gallenblase", "Pankreas", "Milz", "Duodenum"]', 'Gallenblase', 'Die Gallenblase speichert und konzentriert die in der Leber gebildete Galle zwischen den Mahlzeiten. Nach Nahrungsaufnahme wird sie in das Duodenum abgegeben.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('6b258ceb-338b-4159-b7ce-5fa41edc9291', '2a584990-6f61-4085-b124-3186331836c5', 'de', 'Welcher Erreger verursacht häufig peptische Ulzera?', '["Helicobacter pylori", "E. coli", "Salmonella enterica", "Campylobacter jejuni"]', 'Helicobacter pylori', 'Helicobacter pylori kolonisiert die Magenschleimhaut und foerdert dort chronische Entzuendung. Dadurch entstehen haeufig Gastritis und peptische Ulzera.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('0ce16031-bb95-4be5-87c3-9224889601fa', 'f87c115b-fc74-4ab9-aada-ed867985b22c', 'de', 'Wo wird Vitamin B12 hauptsächlich resorbiert?', '["Terminales Ileum", "Duodenum", "Jejunum", "Colon"]', 'Terminales Ileum', 'Vitamin B12 wird hauptsaechlich im terminalen Ileum resorbiert. Voraussetzung dafuer ist die Bindung an Intrinsic Factor aus dem Magen.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('6c479098-42c8-4653-afb4-e25d9e2f3647', 'ce66991c-6ed9-47d6-ac6d-b6221339e9ba', 'de', 'Welche Gerinnungszeit prüft vor allem die extrinsische Kaskade?', '["Quick/INR", "aPTT", "Thrombinzeit", "Blutungszeit"]', 'Quick/INR', 'Quick/INR prueft vor allem die extrinsische Gerinnungskaskade, insbesondere den Faktor VII. Deshalb wird der Wert auch zur Kontrolle einer Vitamin-K-Antagonisten-Therapie genutzt.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('0775a812-a382-49d2-a2ee-820695f95102', 'be5b726d-179d-495d-abb2-04367dab6a67', 'de', 'Welches Vitamin ist bei perniziöser Anämie vermindert?', '["Vitamin B12", "Vitamin C", "Vitamin D", "Vitamin K"]', 'Vitamin B12', 'Bei pernizioeser Anaemie ist Vitamin B12 vermindert, weil durch Intrinsic-Factor-Mangel die Aufnahme im terminalen Ileum gestoert ist. Dadurch entsteht eine megaloblaestaere Anaemie.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('1e8f2d54-657b-4d73-b3e3-7610e21cafd8', '0681a04f-b4ee-42d7-bc83-00812d3d089b', 'de', 'Welcher UV-Bereich verursacht Sonnenbrand am ehesten?', '["UVB", "UVA", "UVC", "Infrarot"]', 'UVB', 'UVB verursacht Sonnenbrand am ehesten, weil diese Strahlung vor allem die Epidermis erreicht und dort direkte DNA-Schaeden ausloest. UVA dringt tiefer ein, ist aber weniger typisch fuer den akuten Sonnenbrand.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('572fb773-8c1c-4153-9516-bc4ad1124e4b', '4c1f4dfd-4c09-4e5f-adc3-5b88089a4bc8', 'de', 'Wie heisst die oberste Hautschicht?', '["Epidermis", "Dermis", "Subkutis", "Faszie"]', 'Epidermis', 'Die Epidermis ist die oberste Hautschicht und bildet die aeussere Barriere des Koerpers. Sie schuetzt vor Keimen, Austrocknung und mechanischen Reizen.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('f40e10d3-b877-4596-828a-d2a08164dc1f', '9a11e1f0-864d-48b8-9b1c-843dcdbd1846', 'de', 'Welcher Erreger verursacht häufig Impetigo contagiosa?', '["Staphylococcus aureus", "Escherichia coli", "Candida albicans", "Mycoplasma pneumoniae"]', 'Staphylococcus aureus', 'Staphylococcus aureus ist ein haeufiger Erreger der Impetigo contagiosa. Der Keim verursacht eine oberflaechliche eitrige Hautinfektion mit typischen honiggelben Krusten.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('29a4a079-25e6-4df2-a039-660dbac4e445', 'd3a4e2d8-a72c-4de8-82a6-17479d4728dc', 'de', 'Welche Struktur sorgt für das scharfe Sehen?', '["Fovea centralis", "Papille", "Glaskörper", "Ziliarkörper"]', 'Fovea centralis', 'Die Fovea centralis ist der Ort des schaerfsten Sehens, weil dort die Dichte der Zapfen am hoechsten ist. Sie ist fuer hochaufgeloestes Farb- und Detailsehen entscheidend.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('9ab3fd07-b3b1-42f3-8b2b-822cd3a3e9e3', 'f5a6e769-9427-4832-a8f0-8974da8aeadf', 'de', 'Welcher Druck ist bei Glaukom typischerweise erhöht?', '["Augeninnendruck", "Blutdruck", "Liquordruck", "Pulsdruck"]', 'Augeninnendruck', 'Beim Glaukom ist der Augeninnendruck haeufig erhoeht, was den Sehnerv langfristig schaedigen kann. Unbehandelt drohen Gesichtsfeldausfaelle bis zur Erblindung.', '2026-01-30 21:45:58.767708+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('f4c3e659-b46f-4f19-9cc9-d9930f442d36', 'ca6e0b05-de4c-4926-bc22-2d70f5362016', 'en', 'Which EKG wave represents the atrial excitation?', '["P-wave", "QRS complex", "T-wave", "U-wave"]', 'P-wave', 'The P wave represents atrial depolarization. Ventricular depolarization follows later in the QRS complex.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('65ee8601-d7ab-4900-99bf-7b55aeecfc0a', 'f3327fb0-011c-4933-b4cd-6ccf13e935ee', 'en', 'Where does the gas exchange take place in the lungs?', '["alveols", "bronchi", "Pleura", "Trachea"]', 'alveols', 'Gas exchange takes place in the alveoli because their blood-air barrier is extremely thin. This allows oxygen to diffuse into blood and carbon dioxide to diffuse into exhaled air.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('8b9d86f1-7d87-4646-996e-fdb66080f13e', '8ed37ab3-18aa-453f-a953-6e7dbb83245f', 'en', 'What muscle is the most important breathing muscle?', '["Plumb", "Intercostal muscles", "M. sternocleidomastoideus", "belly muscles"]', 'Plumb', 'The diaphragm is the main respiratory muscle because its contraction expands the thoracic cavity downward. This lowers intrathoracic pressure and draws air into the lungs.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('9d9fad18-b99f-4433-a638-093dd635b36d', 'f7ab05f5-725e-4dea-a504-8a103329a8cc', 'en', 'Where does ultrafiltration take place in the kidney?', '["Glomerulus", "Henle loop", "Collection tube", "Distal Tubulus"]', 'Glomerulus', 'Ultrafiltration occurs in the glomerulus, where blood is filtered across the glomerular barrier into Bowman''s space. This is how primary urine is formed.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('8dd68e6a-e318-4003-9ef3-636fd0206f3e', '7aaf5d7f-6274-4781-9b68-ef8af0b1b2c0', 'en', 'What structure is crucial for countercurrent multiplication?', '["Henle loop", "Bowman Chapel", "Proximal tube", "Glomerulus"]', 'Henle loop', 'The loop of Henle is essential for countercurrent multiplication because its descending and ascending limbs handle water and salt differently. This creates the osmotic gradient in the renal medulla.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('c4866ab0-618c-4597-877c-0f06390fe13a', '7160d588-e7b7-45d8-9018-1d1ab91b406a', 'en', 'What enzyme is typically increased in cholesterol?', '["Alkaline phosphatase", "amylase", "troponine", "CK-MB"]', 'Alkaline phosphatase', 'Alkaline phosphatase rises in cholestatic liver disease because it is associated mainly with the biliary system. Cholestasis therefore typically leads to elevated ALP levels.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('ccf78a81-ee1b-4dc8-9de0-086c503aeba6', '09f5f514-aae2-4788-b3c1-f3c198fc4cbe', 'en', 'Which toxin is detoxified in the liver to urea?', '["ammonia", "lactate", "Glucose", "bilirubin"]', 'ammonia', 'Ammonia is detoxified in the liver through the urea cycle. This is crucial because free ammonia is neurotoxic and must be converted into more easily excreted urea.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('369a512f-88ab-45ca-a0a9-8c4b4a17e53e', 'd25210b9-a523-49ca-b829-e65d753cbe69', 'en', 'Which brain nerve infiltrates the M. rectus lateralis?', '["N. abducens (VI)", "N. oculomotorius (III)", "N. trochlearis (IV)", "N. trigeminus (V)"]', 'N. abducens (VI)', 'The abducens nerve innervates the lateral rectus muscle and therefore abducts the eye. A lesion prevents proper outward movement of the affected eye.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('836eedc6-ceeb-4b2d-8181-7e52aab6dcf2', 'f9b239c6-b9ff-4aca-bb3d-78ad76eced2b', 'en', 'What gland structure does TSH produce?', '["adenohypophysis", "Neurohypophysis", "Auxiliary mark", "thyroid"]', 'adenohypophysis', 'TSH is produced in the anterior pituitary. From there it stimulates the thyroid gland to synthesize and release T3 and T4.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('5b8d19e8-00cf-45cd-9b6f-75f0c0918e44', 'd763b69b-0d5a-4ba2-b684-1f6de6520e7d', 'en', 'What hormone is formed in the adrenal bark and increases blood pressure?', '["aldosterone", "adrenalin", "inulin", "Glucagon"]', 'aldosterone', 'Aldosterone is produced in the zona glomerulosa of the adrenal cortex. It increases renal sodium and water retention and can therefore raise blood pressure.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('ef22b35f-4d44-4122-9e6f-db2f1749c92b', '46f06b2d-af16-4436-9ec3-13e69bf6a3db', 'en', 'Which hormone promotes the absorption of glucose in cells?', '["inulin", "Glucagon", "cortisol", "adrenalin"]', 'inulin', 'Insulin promotes glucose uptake into cells, especially muscle and adipose tissue. One important mechanism is insertion of GLUT4 transporters into the cell membrane.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('f8a5f9a0-966c-4c62-9ed1-602936b2db44', '5300bc3e-1479-4565-a1f2-ce0910cc9ead', 'en', 'What structure does Galle store?', '["gall bladder", "Pancreas", "spleen", "duodenum"]', 'gall bladder', 'The gallbladder stores and concentrates bile produced by the liver between meals. After food intake, bile is released into the duodenum.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('7340200c-5ca2-471a-a4e2-e379d6f3f184', '2a584990-6f61-4085-b124-3186331836c5', 'en', 'Which pathogen often causes peptic Ulzera?', '["Helicobacter pylori", "E. coli", "Salmonella enterica", "Campylobacter jejuni"]', 'Helicobacter pylori', 'Helicobacter pylori colonizes the gastric mucosa and promotes chronic inflammation there. This is why it commonly causes gastritis and peptic ulcers.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('95cf9246-8c8c-4f13-8cdf-619277a477f8', 'f87c115b-fc74-4ab9-aada-ed867985b22c', 'en', 'Where is vitamin B12 mainly absorbed?', '["Terminals Ileum", "duodenum", "Jejunum", "Colone"]', 'Terminals Ileum', 'Vitamin B12 is absorbed mainly in the terminal ileum. This requires binding to intrinsic factor produced in the stomach.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('cb730bd7-8785-4c39-898a-f3b6a9fe4121', 'ce66991c-6ed9-47d6-ac6d-b6221339e9ba', 'en', 'What coagulation time is the extrinsic cascade?', '["Quick/INR", "aPTT", "Thrombin time", "bleeding time"]', 'Quick/INR', 'PT/INR mainly tests the extrinsic coagulation pathway, especially factor VII. It is therefore also used to monitor vitamin K antagonist therapy.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('a250dd88-006c-4190-be77-7e020d31dc69', 'be5b726d-179d-495d-abb2-04367dab6a67', 'en', 'What vitamin is reduced in pernicious anemia?', '["Vitamin B12", "Vitamin C", "Vitamin D", "Vitamin K"]', 'Vitamin B12', 'In pernicious anemia, vitamin B12 is low because lack of intrinsic factor impairs absorption in the terminal ileum. This leads to a megaloblastic anemia.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('33845615-e909-46ca-adf2-8f16e17692ca', '0681a04f-b4ee-42d7-bc83-00812d3d089b', 'en', 'Which UV range does sunburn most likely cause?', '["UVB", "UVA", "UV", "Infrared"]', 'UVB', 'UVB is most strongly associated with sunburn because it primarily reaches the epidermis and causes direct DNA damage there. UVA penetrates deeper but is less typical for acute sunburn.', '2026-02-01 21:18:30.133289+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('ea1a676f-9087-4a05-899a-3de1f428af71', '4c1f4dfd-4c09-4e5f-adc3-5b88089a4bc8', 'en', 'How does the uppermost skin layer mean?', '["epidermis", "Dermis", "Subcutaneous", "fascia"]', 'epidermis', 'The epidermis is the outermost layer of the skin and forms the body''s external barrier. It protects against pathogens, dehydration, and mechanical stress.', '2026-02-01 21:18:42.211795+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('f97a4dee-913a-498c-ad6f-cebb49bab248', '9a11e1f0-864d-48b8-9b1c-843dcdbd1846', 'en', 'Which pathogen often causes Impetigo contagiosa?', '["Staphylococcus aureus", "Escherichia coli", "Candida albicans", "Mycoplasma pneumonia"]', 'Staphylococcus aureus', 'Staphylococcus aureus is a common cause of impetigo contagiosa. It produces a superficial purulent skin infection with the classic honey-colored crusts.', '2026-02-01 21:18:52.231472+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('d1c26fa7-d72b-4678-92cf-fb3e93859353', 'd3a4e2d8-a72c-4de8-82a6-17479d4728dc', 'en', 'What structure ensures sharp vision?', '["Fovea centralis", "paprika", "Glassware", "ciliary bodies"]', 'Fovea centralis', 'The fovea centralis is the point of sharpest vision because cone density is highest there. It is crucial for fine detail and color vision.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00'),
	('abb8d45c-879c-45ed-8e25-aadef57a71fc', 'f5a6e769-9427-4832-a8f0-8974da8aeadf', 'en', 'What pressure is typically increased in glaucoma?', '["Internal pressure", "Blood pressure", "Liquor pressure", "Pulse pressure"]', 'Internal pressure', 'In glaucoma, intraocular pressure is often elevated and can progressively damage the optic nerve. Without treatment this can cause visual field loss and blindness.', '2026-02-01 21:19:04.163532+00', '2026-03-14 13:27:24.334639+00');
